Bundle-Name: Fennec Services API
Bundle-Description: \
	The contract everything else agrees on: what a broker offers, and \
	what both sides of the wire need to know about the model. The four \
	role interfaces with their diagnostics, event sink and event \
	document; the sd1 and im1 fingerprints; the flavor list convention; \
	deriving a contract from a Java interface. No implementation, no \
	components, no configuration. \
	\
	Deliberately free of the XMI codec. A fingerprint is computed over \
	the in-memory model and never over serialised bytes, so the two only \
	shared a bundle by accident — and keeping them apart is what lets \
	the codec be donated to emf.osgi without taking this project's \
	frozen wire schemes with it.

-library: enableEMF

-buildpath: \
	osgi.core;version=latest,\
	org.eclipse.fennec.services.model;version=snapshot

# ContractAddressing decides what a catalog entry is addressed by, and
# the fingerprints are pinned byte for byte against golden files that
# the TypeScript side reads too.
-testpath: \
	${junit},\
	junit-platform-launcher;version=latest
